pages
mapFunctionsRouting
	^HelpTopic
		title: '6] Routing' "has to be updated manually"
		icon: (HelpIcons iconNamed: #mapPinIcon)
		contents: 'MAP FUNCTIONS: Routing
----------------------------------------------

ROUTING:
To be able to route you need to connect to an API.

    In the lower left corner click on select API and choose one of those available (recommended OpenStreetMaps).
    Next to the select API button is an API key button, where you need to add an API key for the API you selected.
    You have to generate an API key via the website of the respective API (note that some APIs are not free to use).

TO ROUTE:

    First, search for a pin/location in the search bar
    Then click on Directions
    A new interface opens that allows you to specify your route.
    You can select a preferred mode of transportation (walk, bike, car).
    Further, you can add and remove the Hops of your Route. Below the Add Hop and Remove Hop buttons you see a list of all the added Hops (that define your route).
    Add Hop: Type the name of your hop/location in the Add Hop field and click on this button to add the Hop to the list.
    Remove Hop: First click on the Hop in the list and then click on this button to remove the selected Hop.
    If you only choose two Hops, the first one will be the Start and the second one the Destination of your Route.
    --> click Go to route
    By adding more than two Hops you can add intermediary stops to the route. These stops will appear in the list in the order you add them. However, by using the U and D buttons, or 	by drag-and-drop you can reorder the Hops. Clicking on Go will give you the respective routing of that list, but for an optimal route you should click on Find optimal Route.
    To close the routing interface, click on the x (close) button in the upper right corner of the left sidebar.'